Standard implementation. O(n²) runtime, in-place. Code below.

```python
def bubble_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(0, n - i - 1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j + 1]:
                arr[j], arr[j + 1] = arr[j + 1], arr[j]
    return arr
```

Runs until adjacent pairs stop swapping. Fine for light loads; stupid-industrious past a few thousand. If the dataset grows, pivot to a structural fix like Timsort before it burns cycles.
